# Prime Directive

- Prefer security, zero telemetry, and network anonymity in every overlay, package, and daemon change.
- Keep MAC randomization, Quad9 DNS-over-TLS (`9.9.9.9:853`), RFC 4941 IPv6 privacy, and drop-unsolicited firewall posture intact.
- Never put ISO blobs, chroots, `out/`, credentials, or `.env` files in Git.
- Layer work into `packages/`, `build/`, `overlay/`, and `docs/`. Packages must stay `makepkg`-clean.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
git add out/synapseos-2026.10.30-x86_64.iso

# ✅ GOOD
./build/verify-gates.sh
./build/build-iso.sh --dry-run
```
